65,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the most rational choice. The public beds offer a predictable flat rate of 1,100 yen, avoiding the financial risks associated with the non-refundable deposits of a private lodge like Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option C is problematic. Public sports facilities often lack full meal services, which would force the organizers back into the kitchen. Option A, with meals arranged by the owner, is the only way to ensure a fair workload.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option B is out because separate accommodation will only reinforce the year-group divide. Option A is better for integration and labor, but we must ensure the building layout encourages shared evenings.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C is concerning. Based on my research, inland public centers often have overcrowded rooms and strict rules, which could lead to poor sleep and exhaustion. Option A seems more promising for a peaceful environment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is impossible given the hall's timetable. Option A is far, which will cause the transport costs to spike and exacerbate the unfairness of a flat fee. Option C is the most financially stable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, @Jonathan, the risks of Option A are too high. A private lodge two prefectures away with a non-refundable deposit is a financial gamble we cannot afford. Option C is the only stable choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, financial stability is meaningless if the organizers are burnt out. Option C's dorms and lack of catering will repeat last year's failure. Option A's owner-provided meals are the only way to protect our time and health.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, @Asuka, financial stability is important, but the camp's purpose is growth. Option C's dorms might be crowded, but Option A's private building ensures everyone stays together, which is the only way to fix our social fragmentation.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, @Asuka, while I understand the financial concerns, we must not ignore the human cost. If we choose Option C and the rooms are overcrowded, the lack of sleep will ruin the training. Option A offers a more serene environment.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio @Minako, you are prioritizing convenience over fairness. Option A's distance makes the transport cost a massive variable. If we use a flat fee, those who don't travel far effectively subsidize others, which is logically unsound.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka is correct. Option A is a financial liability. @Toshio, we can solve the meal issue by hiring a caterer or adjusting the budget, but we cannot recover a lost deposit. Option C is the only responsible choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, hiring a caterer for a public facility is often logistically impossible or prohibitively expensive. We cannot gamble on ""adjusting the budget"" while ignoring the reality of the labor. Option A is the only sustainable choice for the organizers.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji @Asuka, we cannot let financial caution override the club's health. Option C's dorms risk overcrowding and poor sleep, while Option B fails our members. Option A ensures we stay together and are well-fed, which is essential for integration.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji @Asuka, I understand the budget risks, but we must prioritize the members' well-being. Option C's dormitories are likely too crowded for proper recovery. Option A provides the peace and rest necessary for a successful training camp.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio @Minako @Jonathan, you are ignoring the risk of last-minute cancellations. With Option A's non-refundable deposit, a single dropout creates a financial hole. Option C's public bed system is the only way to ensure no one is unfairly burdened.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Minako"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,The financial risk of Option A is unacceptable. We cannot jeopardize the club account with non-refundable deposits and unpredictable transport costs. Option C is the only choice that ensures stability and fairness. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, stability is a facade if the organizers are sacrificed. I will not support a return to the kitchen. For the sake of sustainability and health, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji @Asuka, financial risk is manageable, but social fragmentation is a systemic failure. Option A provides the unified environment we need to actually integrate the year-groups. For the club's long-term health, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I cannot support Option C, as the risk of overcrowding and sleep deprivation is too high for a productive camp. For the well-being and recovery of all members, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Asuka,,The lack of a clear policy for cancellations and the volatility of transport costs make Option A a logical failure. I cannot support a plan that risks financial inequity. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
